 "prompt": "This 10-block row shuttle is broken: it does not do what it should. Repair it.\n\nGoal: A row of 10 cyan concrete blocks at (1..10, 0, 0) moves one cell east to (2..11, 0, 0) when the lever is switched on and one cell back west when it is switched off.\n\nSpec (checked in the game engine):\n- Lever at [-1, -1, 3]; it starts off. The grader settles the build, then flips the lever 6 times (idle gaps [0, 3, 7, 1, 11, 2] ticks before each flip).\n- After each flip the build must come to rest within 60 ticks, then stay unchanged for 40 ticks.\n- Lever off (start and after every even flip): (1..10, 0, 0) is cyan_concrete; (11, 0, 0) is air or piston_head.\n- Lever on (after every odd flip): (2..11, 0, 0) is cyan_concrete; (1, 0, 0) is air or piston_head.\n- The whole build must return to exactly the same resting state every two flips; no item drops; no block may leave the box.\n- At most 62 blocks (lever included), all inside the box [-2, -3, -1]..[15, 1, 4].\n- Exactly 10 cyan_concrete in the build, at all times.\n- These cells must stay empty at every tick: [[[1, 11], 1, 0], [[1, 11], 0, -1]].\n\nYou may change, add or remove any blocks except the lever. Allowed blocks: the benchmark allow-list. Submit the complete build as a list of blocks.",
 "verified": true
}